  "overview": "Dr. Jonghwa Oh received a MS (2008) in Environmental Engineering from Yonsei University in Korea, with a focus on noise and vibration. She earned a MPH (2012) and PhD (2016) in Environmental Health Sciences (Industrial Hygiene track) from UAB. She is currently an assistant professor in the Department of Environmental Health Sciences at UAB and the  director of the Industrial Hygiene program in the NIOSH funded Deep South Center for Occupational Health and Safety.",
